eeBasename","reason":"pins SessionName deriving the session name as the worktree's basename; its covering tests run this code without asserting it"},{"name":"TestSessionReapRoots","reason":"pins that Down's reap roots exclude a dead pane's recorded pid, a pid-less pane and a corpse-only session; its covering tests run this code without asserting it"},{"name":"TestStageLaunchScript_WriteFailureDegrades","reason":"pins an unwritable launch directory returning the composed line unchanged and logging the strand and script path; its covering tests run this code without asserting it"},{"name":"TestStrandNameLocked_Names","reason":"pins how an add forms its strand name: the role numbered by the strands holding it, a dormant strand still counting, a legacy name holding nothing, an empty slug giving two segments and an empty role defaulting to strand; its covering tests run this code without asserting it"},{"name":"TestStripIdentityEnv_DropsNameParentAndRunMarkOnly","reason":"pins the pane env dropping exactly LYM_STRAND_NAME, LYM_PARENT and LYM_RUN_PROCESS and keeping a longer key sharing the prefix; its covering tests run this code without asserting it"},{"name":"TestTruncateAtRuneBoundary","reason":"pins the readable half of the socket key being cut at a rune boundary: under or at the limit untouched, a straddling rune dropped whole, zero keeps nothing, always valid UTF-8; its covering tests run this code without asserting it"},{"name":"TestValidateIfAbsent","reason":"pins --if-absent requiring a name: rejected naming --name when IfAbsent is set without one, accepted otherwise; its covering tests run this code without asserting it"},{"name":"TestValidateSplitCreatedNewPane","reason":"pins the genuinely-new-pane guard: a fresh pane id passes while an empty, pre-existing alive or pre-existing dead pane id errors; its covering tests run this code without asserting it"},{"name":"TestWatchdogOption","reason":"pins the watchdog option validating and normalizing: on and off in any case or padding, and an empty, numeric, true, yes or misspelled value rejected naming the offending value; its covering tests run this code without asserting it"},{"name":"TestWatchdogTemplateDefault_BothGOOS","reason":"pins both embedded templates and the shipped accessor declaring the watchdog default line, reading the posix and windows files directly since ConfigTemplate exposes only one; its covering tests run this code without asserting it"},{"name":"TestWithOpLock_PathIsUnderDotLym","reason":"pins the lock file living under the anchor path's .lym, not the worktree root's, for a subpath-anchored fixture, and a second acquisition succeeding after release; its covering tests run this code without asserting it"},{"name":"TestWithOpLock_SerializesConcurrentCalls","reason":"pins a second withOpLock blocking until the first releases and then proceeding; its covering tests run this code without asserting it"},{"name":"TestWithTryOpLock","reason":"pins withTryOpLock running fn on a free lock with acquired true, wrapping fn's error with acquired still true, and deferring with (false, nil) and no fn call or tmux call while the lock is held; its covering tests run this code without asserting it"}],"map_built_at":"2026-11-16T10:55:57+01:00","map_commit":"894abe594a3272b1f94f362c0e427f0f6e7d7163","not_judged":[{"name":"TestCheckTmuxFloor_RunsNoProbeOnWindows","reason":"failed"},{"name":"TestSelvageIdentifiersConfinedToSelvagePane","reason":"no blocks"},{"name":"TestShowToggleOutcome","reason":"unclassifiable call"},{"name":"TestStatusFormatActions_SlackAndAwayTogglesFollowTheFollowButton","reason":"no blocks"},{"name":"TestStatusFormats_SessionLoopsTakeOneFormat","reason":"no blocks"},{"name":"TestTmuxProcessName","reason":"failed"}],"ok":true,"package":"internal/reedengine","tests":196}
